 did a bunch of takes but but at least  we've gotten the we we recorded the  music already so we're playing it but  then we you know as we're filming its  immune it's impossibly impossible to do  it any other way I think it's abundantly  clear that Bradley is very naturally  talented when it comes to his musical  abilities but this is taking it to  another level so I kind of want to steal  whatever advice you gave him especially  with the guitar because I've played  saxophone all my life and then I wanted  to play guitar but there's just  something about it that never really  clicked so is there any piece of advice  that you gave him that might help other  aspiring artists out there what I know  is that when you have an ear for music  if you can hear what the right tone is  the right note if you can if you can  recognize the right note then you're the  battles already won and it's just a  matter of training yourself to produce  that note and and you know and that's  just muscle memory in you know your your  voice your throat is an instrument in  itself and you know your hands are  muscles that can be can manipulate an  instrument in order to produce a certain  note so all you have to do is be able to  hear if it sounds good and that's the  battle so for singing do you believe  that if someone can hear the note they  can no matter what actually oh yeah  absolutely not' I can't sing for [ __ ]  but that's because you haven't practiced  in the right way okay yeah okay maybe  maybe we could sit down whenever you're  free okay thank you so much  [Music]
 

